<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/adaptive-testing> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "ERIC scope note: Testing that involves selecting test items according to the examinee's ability as shown by responses to earlier test items" <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/adaptive-testing/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/adaptive-testing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://glossarystudio.app/ns/Definition> <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/adaptive-testing/versions/1> .
<https://id.i2idl.org/definitions/adaptive-testing> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#value> "Assessment that selects or adjusts subsequent test items in response to information from a learner’s earlier answers." <https://id.i2idl.org/graphs/concepts/adaptive-testing/versions/1> .
